  "title": "Adjusted data type for 3GPP-Session-Stop-Indicator",
  "description": "3GPP-Session-Stop-Indicator is currently specified as UTF8String but I believe it should be OctetString instead.\nThis AVP has been defined in [ETSI TS 129 061](https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/129000_129099/129061/19.01.00_60/ts_129061v190100p.pdf) where it mentions the AVP is \"Bit String type\" and \"Value is set to all 1\". Indeed, the only valid value for this AVP is a single byte 0xFF. In wireshark radius dictionary this is correctly listed as byte.\n\nHowever, in diameter dictionary this is listed as UTF8String which is incorrect as equivalend of the RADIUS byte data type is OctetString and not UTF8String. In addition, 0xFF (which is the only valid value for this AVP) is not a valid UTF-8 text and thus it can never be parsed correctly. Indeed, Wireshark currently decodes it as \"�\" which is replacement character when decoding fails.\n\nI would propose changing data type to OctetString as it more closely reflects the intended data type and it properly supports the only valie this AVP can have (0xFF).\n\nThis is how this AVP is currently parsed:\n ![current-3gpp-session-stop-indicator](/uploads/d000a5becb86ca2419b1d2f1243d2a22/current-3gpp-session-stop-indicator.png){width=468 height=146}\n\nThis is how I believe this AVP should be parsed:\n ![corrected-3gpp-session-stop-indicator](/uploads/3adbf143198e04570c590e881c420985/corrected-3gpp-session-stop-indicator.png){width=463 height=145}",
